<title>CHILE: Chile boosts first half copper price estimate.</title>
<headline>Chile boosts first half copper price estimate.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chilean government has revised upward its estimate of the average price of copper in the first half of the year to $1.10 per pound, from $1.00 previously, Mining Minister Benjamin Teplizky said.</p>
<p>The readujstment was made in line with recent gains in prices for the red metal, Teplizky told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;The projection now is about $1.10 for the first half of the year,&quot; he said. The copper price average is used in both public and private finances in Chile as a key economic indicator.</p>
<p>He declined to project a price for the second half of the year.</p>
<p>((--Paulina Modiano, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
